# content-seal drives the recorder hook and the seal library it sources (every seal row), and the three
# join readers that compare against it. Without the two seal files declared, the sandbox omits them and
# every arm runs the absent-sibling path, so both are REQUIRED. The arm scripts borrow the worlds of
# adversarial-shard-merge and remediator-shard-join by sourcing their lib.sh, so those directories and
# every sibling those libs check at startup are declared too.
!core/scripts/content-seal.sh
!core/hooks/ai-dlc-content-seal.sh
!core/scripts/merge-adversarial-shards.sh
!core/scripts/join-remediator-shards.sh
!core/scripts/validate-gate-adjudication.sh
# --mark / --mark-repair, the one sanctioned Bash write into the sealed set (arms CS-K*, CS-J6..J9).
!core/scripts/wait-for-deliverable.sh
core/scripts/validate-adversarial-convergence.sh
core/scripts/validate-steering-budget.sh
core/scripts/validate-suppression-lifetime.sh
core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh
core/scripts/validate-artifact-derivations.sh
core/scripts/validate-provenance-block.sh
core/scripts/partition-document.sh
core/scripts/partition-subject.sh
core/schemas/provenance-block.json
core/schemas/gate-adjudication-verdict.json
core/skills/ai-dlc/enforcement-map.yaml
core/team-roles/remediator.md
# BL-750: the CURRENT-state adversary role file the marker-admission arms (CS-A*) copy into their worlds.
!core/team-roles/adversary.md
core/hooks/ai-dlc-gate-remediation-guard.sh
core/hooks/ai-dlc-derivation-capture.sh
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/
core/fixtures/remediator-shard-join/
core/fixtures/lib/
